{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791218046,"nonce":"HqFoXBG2Z9Ea5B1Mv4o5kJltKsk=","title":"Minor collection pauses grow with the old heap (86-107ms at 500-600MB), stalling frames","message":"A frame-driven program with a large long-lived heap stalls for a whole collection pause every few seconds. The pauses are labelled minor, but they grow as the live heap grows between full collections, so they get worse the longer the program runs.\n\n**Seen in**\nashui's Studio3D flight demo (a 3D scene at 60fps, about 0.7MB allocated per frame after ashui cut its own allocation): minor collections every ~8s with pause= rising 16ms -\u003e 91ms as live goes 344MB -\u003e 533MB, each one a dropped frame. ASH_GC_STATS shows mark time dominating (e.g. stop=0.01ms mark=59.24ms sweep=6.34ms) and the minor's old roots growing (422432 -\u003e 621636).\n\n**Reproducer** (no ashui; Main.hx below)\n\n    haxe -main Main -hl main.hl\n    ASH_GC_STATS=1 ash main.hl 40\n\nA 300MB graph of small objects stays alive; each simulated 60Hz frame allocates ~700KB of short-lived objects and repoints 300 old objects at new ones.\n\n**Ash** (local release build, hybrid, M-series Mac, 2026-10-05):\n- minor collections every ~7s\n- pause=90.92ms live=518.3MB, 85.71ms at 545.9MB, 106.00ms at 576.8MB, 106.87ms at 605.9MB\n- worst frame in the second of each collection 114-137ms; otherwise ~25ms (the interpreter's own allocation cost)\n\n**Stock HashLink 1.15** (NUC, ~/hashlink/hl): ~125ms pauses nearly every second (worst frames 123-132ms at t=30,31,32,34,35,37,38,39s). So Ash is already far better in frequency; the remaining problem is the size of each pause and its growth.\n\n**What would help a frame loop**\n- a minor's mark proportional to the young generation and the dirty old blocks, not the whole remembered set as it grows;\n- or incremental / time-sliced marking, or a full collection scheduled when the program is idle (the idle collector already exists: here the window thread is not idle long enough between frames);\n- old garbage reclaimed before the live heap grows by ~30MB per collection.\n\n**Main.hx**\n\n    /**\n    \tFrame pauses from collections, without ashui. A long-lived graph of\n    \t`OLD_MB` megabytes of small objects stays alive; each simulated frame\n    \tallocates about 700KB of short-lived objects and repoints a few hundred\n    \told objects at new ones, as a 3D scene's per-frame state does. Prints the\n    \tslowest frame in each second and how many frames passed 25ms.\n    **/\n    class Node {\n    \tpublic var next:Null\u003cNode\u003e;\n    \tpublic var payload:Array\u003cFloat\u003e;\n    \n    \tpublic function new(next, n:Int) {\n    \t\tthis.next = next;\n    \t\tpayload = [for (i in 0...n) i * 0.5];\n    \t}\n    }\n    \n    class Main {\n    \tstatic inline var OLD_MB = 300;\n    \tstatic inline var FRAME_KB = 700;\n    \n    \tstatic function main() {\n    \t\tvar seconds = Std.parseInt(Sys.args().length \u003e 0 ? Sys.args()[0] : \"40\");\n    \t\t// About 150 bytes a node with its payload.\n    \t\tvar old:Array\u003cNode\u003e = [];\n    \t\tvar count = Std.int(OLD_MB * 1024 * 1024 / 200);\n    \t\tfor (i in 0...count)\n    \t\t\told.push(new Node(i \u003e 0 ? old[i - 1] : null, 8));\n    \t\tSys.println('old graph: $count nodes');\n    \t\tvar start = haxe.Timer.stamp(), last = start, second = 0, worst = 0.0, slow = 0, frames = 0;\n    \t\tvar seed = 1;\n    \t\twhile (last - start \u003c seconds) {\n    \t\t\t// Short-lived: what a frame's drawing allocates and drops.\n    \t\t\tvar keep:Null\u003cNode\u003e = null;\n    \t\t\tfor (i in 0...Std.int(FRAME_KB * 1024 / 150))\n    \t\t\t\tkeep = new Node(keep, 8);\n    \t\t\t// A few hundred old objects pointed at new ones: the old generation is dirtied every frame.\n    \t\t\tfor (i in 0...300) {\n    \t\t\t\tseed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) \u0026 0x7fffffff;\n    \t\t\t\told[seed % old.length].next = new Node(null, 4);\n    \t\t\t}\n    \t\t\t// About a 60Hz frame.\n    \t\t\tSys.sleep(0.012);\n    \t\t\tvar now = haxe.Timer.stamp();\n    \t\t\tvar dt = (now - last) * 1000;\n    \t\t\tlast = now;\n    \t\t\tframes++;\n    \t\t\tif (dt \u003e worst)\n    \t\t\t\tworst = dt;\n    \t\t\tif (dt \u003e 25)\n    \t\t\t\tslow++;\n    \t\t\tif (Std.int(now - start) != second) {\n    \t\t\t\tsecond = Std.int(now - start);\n    \t\t\t\tSys.println('t=${second}s worst frame ${Math.round(worst)}ms, frames over 25ms so far $slow of $frames');\n    \t\t\t\tworst = 0;\n    \t\t\t}\n    \t\t}\n    \t}\n    }","files":null}]}